Title: LocoCisco — Every Voice Understood

====================================================================
**CRITICAL — FIXED CAMERA FOR THE ENTIRE VIDEO.**
**The camera is LOCKED OFF on a tripod and NEVER MOVES.**
**ABSOLUTELY NO camera movement of any kind: NO pan, NO tilt, NO**
**tracking, NO dolly, NO handheld drift, NO push-in, and — above all —**
**NO ZOOM. Not at any point, not even slightly.**
**One single static wide shot, held unchanged from the first frame to**
**the last. Only the people and the on-screen overlays move within the**
**frame. The frame itself is completely still.**
====================================================================

INT. CORPORATE CONFERENCE ROOM - DAY

CAMERA: A single locked-off, static camera holds one fixed wide shot for the **entire** video. The framing **never** changes — **no** panning, tilting, tracking, dollying, handheld movement, or **zoom**. Only the people and the on-screen overlays move within the frame.

VIEWPOINT: The camera is positioned INSIDE the room at one END of the conference table, roughly at seated eye level, looking straight down the length of the table toward the far end wall. That far wall — the wall the camera faces and the backdrop behind the table — is a plain wall with a single clean, blank whiteboard on it (nothing written or drawn). From this fixed vantage, WEI and LING sit along the left side of the table and ALEX and JORDAN along the right side, facing each other across it, with the clean whiteboard wall centered in the background.

A wide, balanced view looks down the length of a conference table. WEI, a Chinese man in his 50s, and LING, a younger Chinese woman, sit together on the left in formal suits. ALEX, a man around 30, and JORDAN, a woman around 30, sit opposite in business casual blazers. The far end wall behind the table holds a single clean, blank whiteboard; soft daylight, laptops, and a printed deal sheet give the room a corporate look. Their faces show natural skin texture and subtle expressions. A small LOCOCISCO speaker and caption screen sit between the parties.

**The two parties sit facing each other across the table. Every character directs their gaze and their words to the people seated opposite them — they talk TO EACH OTHER, never to the camera. No character ever looks at, turns to, or addresses the camera at any point; the camera is a neutral observer, and eyelines stay on the other people in the room.**

**OVERLAY RULE — applies EVERY time ANY character speaks (and only while they are speaking): the instant a character begins to talk, a thin rectangle appears over their head, framing their face, and that character's first name appears on a label directly beneath the rectangle. The overlay tracks their head and disappears the moment they stop speaking. This happens for every spoken line, for every character, without exception.**

Ling glances at Wei. Wei gives a subtle nod, his eyes on Alex and Jordan across the table.

Wei looks directly across the table at Alex and Jordan as he speaks. A rectangle appears over Wei's head with WEI on a label beneath it.

WEI
(in Mandarin)
如果价格降百分之十，我们今天签约。

The English translation appears on the caption screen.

LOCOCISCO (V.O.)
If you reduce the price by ten percent, we can sign today.

Jordan leans close to Alex, speaking only to him. Her lips move in a whisper too faint to make out. A rectangle appears over Jordan's head with JORDAN on a label beneath it while she whispers. The caption screen stays blank and the speaker stays silent. Alex gives Jordan a slight nod.

Alex turns to face Wei and Ling across the table and addresses them directly. A rectangle appears over Alex's head with ALEX on a label beneath it.

ALEX
Agreed, if delivery starts next month.

The Mandarin translation appears on the caption screen.

LOCOCISCO (V.O.)
(in Mandarin)
同意，前提是下个月开始交付。

Wei and Ling exchange a brief look. Wei nods to Alex across the table.

Fade to black

ON SCREEN: "LocoCisco — Every voice understood."

====================================================================
**REMINDER: The camera never moved. One fixed, locked-off wide shot**
**for the whole video — NO movement, NO zoom, start to finish.**
====================================================================
